ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8060" :question/id #uuid "e53a5dab-4c76-5167-b8bb-303aab059a57" :question/math-academy-id "q-8060" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/assets/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we compute the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/assets/4a83673a409fd2e5d33b0b5f743f57af08cfb27c38e312a636179102c2172b04.png)\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a reflection in the line $y=-x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8060/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8060"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11952/selection/354549e05d30f5acb6c9a5e876a1b220679b1daee3381277145bd16fe273c514" :answer/id #uuid "b8bab251-cb0c-584a-a750-3e092abd1d93" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Reflection across the $x$-axis" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11952/selection/88080c403df57be69aa0dfa2a3b166fae5b686532c52e30c66ca86c12b4c2b62" :answer/id #uuid "2a9abb55-bc72-5d