by the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=2.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11952/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11952"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78294/selection/8d5f83736d3858f9c8fda9ea57f6e2fce009e11b0eb7c861b2f6a48fbd8d6b21" :answer/id #uuid "15e6e112-c815-5ed5-8970-49bdd7de8243" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78294/selection/2300d797ad41573df5543fb77d48add0501450974497dcca671b3be3b91c8f47" :answer/id #uuid "1f5668ed-596e-55fc-a3af-a7286eb75b61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{12} & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78294/selection/765f5ce688c0deae1f22892107a4359df9eb39808b2acd6c529b1f10beffe3c1" :answer/id #uuid "7cd67797-542c-5d94-928e-afb3cc9afe4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{12} \\\\ \\frac{1}{12} & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78294/selection/16adff7243ace02d5803d28c725587af699cac00bbc2a8c5385b87e7266eac14" :answer/id #uuid "95049707-6db7-5ff1-a0e5-147feff8ff65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78294/selection/817223bdf9a18b51d3b90fe694e74414dbf9c9e0a57563af3b5070495f395b36" :answer/id #uuid "6a57babd-3e4c-5757-808f-68a7b73abd71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{12} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78294/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e3ed604-4dc5-5907-b00f-d0bbba84e2a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78294/selection/817223bdf9a18b51d3b90fe694e74414dbf9c9e0a57563af3b5070495f395b36" :answer-field/choices ["q-78294/selection/8d5f83736d3858f9c8fda9ea57f6e2fce009e11b0eb7c861b2f6a48fbd8d6b21" "q-78294/selection/2300d797ad41573df5543fb77d48add0501450974497dcca671b3be3b91c8f47" "q-78294/selection/765f5ce688c0deae1f22892107a4359df9eb39808b2acd6c529b1f10beffe3c1" "q-78294/selection/16adff7243ace02d5803d28c725587af699cac00bbc2a8c5385b87e7266eac14" "q-78294/selection/817223bdf9a18b51d3b90fe694e74414dbf9c9e0a57563af3b5070495f395b36"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78294" :question/id #uuid "7309edc8-4532-58c0-ac70-deeef25e93b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-78294" :question/problem "A linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation.  Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}60 \\\\ 144\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}60 \\\\ 144\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=\\frac{1}{12}v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=\\frac{1}{12}.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{12} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78294/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78294"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159762/selection/6913df9b151f2261420536f52f0de81cdd0d