 "q-159762" :question/id #uuid "f832c1fd-472d-59a5-a8ed-2070a54406a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-159762" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/assets/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we compute the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/assets/dbe3773dea369f6b58fc2ad45a32f98c2c9ae356701baf3ab56af3daa6ca732d.png)\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a reflection across the $x$-axis." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-159762/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159762"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328229/field-1/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "00c40276-1039-5644-b453-0c176a5b72b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328229/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c64baf7e-97b8-5828-a76c-c33e89e895e0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct